From: PonWrt <ponwrt@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 7 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: share one fallback MAC base across GDMs

airoha_alloc_gdm_device() calls eth_hw_addr_random() for every GDM
independently whenever of_get_ethdev_address() fails, so each port ends up
with an unrelated random OUI:

    gdm1 -> 36:f7:1d:aa:bb:cc
    gdm3 -> 9e:41:02:dd:ee:ff

airoha_set_macaddr() then rejects the second device, because the hardware
requires every GDM that shares a LAN/WAN side to use the same three most
significant bytes:

    gdm3: wrong mac addr, MSBs must be 36:f7:1d
    FE hw forwarding won't work properly

and returns -EINVAL, which disables front-end hardware forwarding.

This is reachable on boards whose MAC storage the kernel cannot read, e.g.
FiberHome HG5580A: its "identity" MTD partition is still erased (all 0xff)
on units that never finished a vendor first boot.  All-0xff fails
is_valid_ether_addr() because 0xff is a multicast address, so both the DT
property lookup and the nvmem cell lookup fail and the random fallback runs.

Randomise one base per controller into struct airoha_eth and hand out
consecutive addresses from it, varying only the low byte per port.  All GDMs
now share the OUI, ports stay distinguishable, and the locally-administered
bit remains set as eth_hw_addr_random() intends.  addr_assign_type is set to
NET_ADDR_RANDOM so the address is still reported as randomised.

Signed-off-by: PonWrt <ponwrt@example.invalid>
---

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -767,6 +767,15 @@
 
 	struct net_device *napi_dev;
 
+	/* Fallback MAC base for GDMs that have no usable address in DT or
+	 * in nvmem.  airoha_set_macaddr() requires every GDM on the same
+	 * LAN/WAN side to share the three most significant bytes, so the
+	 * base is randomised once per controller and each port only varies
+	 * the low byte.
+	 */
+	u8 fallback_mac_base[ETH_ALEN];
+	bool fallback_mac_base_valid;
+
 	struct airoha_qdma qdma[AIROHA_MAX_NUM_QDMA];
 	struct airoha_gdm_port *ports[AIROHA_MAX_NUM_GDM_PORTS];
 };
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -4567,6 +4567,7 @@
 	struct airoha_gdm_dev *dev;
 	int err, i;
 	u8 index;
+	u8 fallback_addr[ETH_ALEN];
 
 	netdev = devm_alloc_etherdev_mqs(eth->dev, sizeof(*dev),
 					 AIROHA_NUM_NETDEV_TX_RINGS,
@@ -4595,9 +4596,27 @@
 		if (err == -EPROBE_DEFER)
 			return err;
 
-		eth_hw_addr_random(netdev);
-		dev_info(eth->dev, "generated random MAC address %pM\n",
-			 netdev->dev_addr);
+		/* airoha_set_macaddr() refuses GDMs that disagree on the three
+		 * most significant MAC bytes, which is exactly what independent
+		 * per-port randomisation produces.  Randomise one base per
+		 * controller instead and give each port a distinct low byte.
+		 */
+		if (!eth->fallback_mac_base_valid) {
+			eth_random_addr(eth->fallback_mac_base);
+			eth->fallback_mac_base_valid = true;
+		}
+
+		ether_addr_copy(fallback_addr, eth->fallback_mac_base);
+		fallback_addr[ETH_ALEN - 1] =
+			eth->fallback_mac_base[ETH_ALEN - 1] +
+			(port->id << 2) + nbq;
+
+		eth_hw_addr_set(netdev, fallback_addr);
+		netdev->addr_assign_type = NET_ADDR_RANDOM;
+
+		dev_info(eth->dev,
+			 "GDM%u has no usable MAC, using %pM (base %pM)\n",
+			 port->id, fallback_addr, eth->fallback_mac_base);
 	}
 
 	/* Allowed nbq for EN7581 on GDM3 port are 4 and 5 for PCIE0
-- 
2.43.0
